        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 23, \"total_count\": 23, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Sellers cannot attach their own photos — no file upload exists\", \"actual\": \"The Create Listing form's photo control is a button \\\"Add Photo\\\" with helper text \\\"Click to add sample images (up to 4)\\\"; it inserts hard-coded Unsplash sample URLs (e.g. images.unsplash.com/photo-1555041469...). There is no input[type=file] anywhere in the form, so a seller can never attach a photo of their actual item. All other submitted data (title, description, $48, Furniture, Good, Austin TX, Upcycled) was retained and displayed correctly on /product/prod-1787827574220.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit capability for existing listings\", \"actual\": \"On /my-listings the only actions for an owned listing are View, Mark Sold and Delete (button list: New Listing, View, Mark Sold, Delete). The owned product page offers only \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\". The account menu contains My Profile / My Listings / Log out (My Profile leads to a 404). There is no UI anywhere to change a listing's title, description, photos, price, category, condition, location or upcycled status.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Emma Green on /my-listings: \\\"Mark Sold\\\" on prod-5 → toast \\\"Item marked as sold\\\", badge changed Active→Sold and the button became \\\"Mark Available\\\"; clicking it → toast \\\"Item marked as available\\\", badge back to Active. \\\"Delete\\\" opened alertdialog \\\"Delete listing? This action cannot be undone.\\\" with Cancel/Delete; confirming showed toast \\\"Listing deleted\\\" and the card disappeared from My Listings immediately (only Mid-Century Modern Armchair left).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After marking prod-5 sold, browse dropped from \\\"10 items available\\\" to 9 with prod-5 absent, and the /categories Home Decor count fell to 1. Its product page showed \\\"This item is no longer available\\\" and offered no Add to Cart / Message Seller (ProductDetail renders the action block only when product.isAvailable, for any viewer). After deleting the listing, browse again shows 9 items and prod-5 is gone entirely.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered Tester One / tester.one@example.com / abc123 / Austin, TX → toast \\\"Account created successfully!\\\", redirected to /, header now shows Sell + account menu (signed in). 5-char password was not accepted.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No maximum-price filter — price range slider exposes only a minimum thumb\", \"actual\": \"The \\\"Price Range\\\" control renders a single Radix thumb with aria-label=\\\"Minimum\\\" (min 0, max 500); moving it to 250 changed the label to \\\"$250 - $500\\\" and returned only items priced >= $250, so the upper bound is permanently fixed at $500 and a buyer cannot cap the price. All other criteria worked: Furniture+condition New+Upcycled-only → exactly prod-10 and prod-3; Max Distance 1 mi → 0 items; sorts verified against underlying data (Newest = dates 11-23…11-10 desc, Price Low→High = 35,45,55,65,95,125,175,180,285,320, Distance = 2.5,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,12,15 asc).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"DENIM\\\"→1 result (prod-2, title match, case-insensitive); \\\"portland\\\"→3 (prod-10/3/8, location match); \\\"cork\\\"→1 (prod-7, description-only match); clearing→\\\"10 items available\\\" with all 10 cards restored.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Signed in as Buyer Test: added prod-1 (Emma Green's $285 armchair) twice → cart badge stayed 1 (no duplicate); added prod-6 ($95) → badge 2. /cart shows \\\"2 items\\\" with photo, title, location (Brooklyn, NY / San Francisco, CA) and price for each, Total $380.00 = 285+95.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Buyer Test on prod-1 (Emma Green's listing): \\\"Message Seller\\\" opened dialog \\\"Send a message to Emma Green\\\"; Send Message was disabled while the textarea was empty; after typing a message it submitted and showed toast \\\"Message sent to seller!\\\" and closed the dialog.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category selection does not filter the browse results\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Home Decor\\\" (1 item) on /categories navigated to /?category=home-decor but the browse page still listed all 9 available items (prod-10, prod-3, prod-1, prod-7, prod-2, prod-8, prod-4, prod-9, prod-6) and reported \\\"9 items available\\\"; no category checkbox was checked. Re-checked after 1.2 s — unchanged. Expected only the Home Decor listing (prod-8) and a count of 1.\", \"evidence\": \"Category tiles on /categories show correct available counts (Furniture 3, Clothing 1, Electronics 1, Home Decor 1, Books 1, Sports 1, Toys 1, Other 0).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No seller view for purchase requests, and cart \\\"requests sent\\\" confirmation records nothing\", \"actual\": \"As Emma Green (seller of prod-1, which had received both a Message-Seller request and a cart purchase request from Buyer Test) there is nowhere to see the requested item or buyer message: /my-listings shows only View/Mark Sold/Delete per listing, the account menu has only My Profile (404)/My Listings/Log out, and App.tsx defines only the routes /, /product/:id, /login, /register, /create-listing, /my-listings, /cart, /about, /categories, *. Additionally Cart.tsx's Send Purchase Request handler only calls toast.success('Purchase requests sent to sellers!') and clearCart() — it never calls the context's sendPurchaseRequest, so the confirmation is shown although no request is recorded for any cart item.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Login with nobody@notregistered.com rejected: \\\"Invalid credentials. Try: emma@example.com\\\"; stayed on /login, header still shows Log in/Sign up.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registering \\\"Fake Emma\\\" with EMMA@example.com (case-only variation of the existing emma@example.com) was rejected with \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\"; afterwards signing in as emma@example.com still yields the original account (avatar/name \\\"Emma Green\\\", her listings intact), so the existing account was not replaced.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is never verified — any password authenticates a registered account\", \"actual\": \"Account buyer.test@example.com was registered with password \\\"buypass123\\\". After logging out, signing in with \\\"totallyWrongPassword\\\" succeeded: toast \\\"Welcome back!\\\", redirect to /, header shows Sell + avatar \\\"Buyer Test\\\" (authenticated session created). The login page even advertises \\\"(any password works)\\\".\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Signed in as Emma Green viewing Sofia Martinez's prod-7: only \\\"Add to Cart\\\" and \\\"Message Seller\\\" are offered — no Mark Sold/Delete/Manage. On her own listing the buyer actions are replaced by \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\", and /my-listings lists only the signed-in user's own items (Emma: prod-1 + prod-5) each with View/Mark Sold/Delete.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit blocked (title/description/price/location are required inputs with native \\\"Please fill out this field.\\\" messages; category/condition selects also required). With all fields filled but no image, submit blocked with toast \\\"Please add at least one image\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Price input is type=number min=0; submitting -10 blocked submission (stayed on /create-listing, no listing created) with validation message \\\"Value must be greater than or equal to 0.\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Protected routes render a blank page instead of a sign-in prompt or redirect\", \"actual\": \"While signed out, /create-listing, /cart and /my-listings each render an empty document (document.body.innerText === \\\"\\\", #root contains only the toast container) and stay on that URL — no sign-in prompt, no redirect, no explanation. In-app entry points do behave correctly: the Sell button is hidden when signed out, \\\"Add to Cart\\\" on a product redirects to /login, and \\\"Message Seller\\\" opens a dialog with a \\\"Log in to message\\\" button. So the actions are blocked, but direct/unauthenticated access to the protected pages leaves the user on a blank screen.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting EMMA@Example.com showed immediate inline error \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\"; form stayed on /register with values retained and editable (subsequently corrected to register a new account).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing character-by-character (pressSequentially) updated the grid and the \\\"N items available\\\" counter live with no search button/Enter; clearing the box immediately restored \\\"10 items available\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each change applied instantly with no submit: Furniture → \\\"3 items available\\\"; +New → then +Upcycled → \\\"2 items available\\\"; price min 250 → 2 items; distance 1 mi → \\\"0 items available\\\"; sort switches (Price Low→High, Distance) reordered the grid immediately. \\\"Clear all filters\\\" reset every checkbox/slider and restored \\\"10 items available\\\" with 10 cards.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each Add to Cart produced an immediate \\\"Added to cart!\\\" toast and the header cart badge incremented live (0→1→2) with no reload; the cart page then listed both line items and Total $380.00 consistent with the additions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"prod-1 detail matched its underlying data exactly (multi-image carousel with dots, \\\"Mid-Century Modern Armchair\\\", full description, $285, Furniture, Like New, \\\"Brooklyn, NY (2.5 mi)\\\", seller Emma Green / Brooklyn NY, \\\"Listed 2024-11-20\\\", Upcycled badge — data: price 285, category furniture, condition like-new, isUpcycled true, createdAt 2024-11-20, seller user-1). prod-7 (non-upcycled) correctly showed no Upcycled badge. Availability is reflected by state: available listings expose Add to Cart/Message Seller, while the sold prod-5 showed \\\"This item is no longer available\\\". A newly created listing likewise showed its own title/description/price/category/condition/location/date/upcycled badge and seller.\"}]}"
